ReliKey composes, without modification, upstream images that keep their own licences. Each runs as its own
container; ReliKey links none of them into its code:
  Keycloak        - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak
  Broker database - PostgreSQL - https://www.postgresql.org
  Front proxy     - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/caddyserver/caddy
  KeyClerk        - EUPL-1.2   - https://github.com/keyclerk/keyclerk
  Warpgate        - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/warp-tech/warpgate
  LDAP facade     - GPL-3.0    - https://github.com/lldap/lldap
  Update mirror   - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/project-zot/zot

Optional, not shipped: OpenBao (MPL-2.0, https://github.com/openbao/openbao), read by Warpgate when an
organisation runs one.

